43su|n|A large, amphibious, herbivorous mammal (Hippopotamus amphibius), common in the rivers of Africa. It is allied to the hogs, and has a very thick, naked skin, a thick and square head, a very large muzzle, small eyes and ears, thick and heavy body, and short legs. It is supposed to be the behemoth of the Bible. Called also zeekoe, and river horse. A smaller species (H. Liberiencis) inhabits Western Africa.	n:43su,165,10;81mj,150,5;unn,132,3;5a8p,78,3;19w4,48,3;1jlg,18,6;alxf,13,1~43su,165,10;1jlg,18,6;81mj,150,5;5a8p,78,3;19w4,48,3;unn,132,3;alxf,13,1	N:43su,165,10;3c17,151,4;29i5,96,3;5726,93,3;29iv,87,6~43su,165,10;29iv,87,6;3c17,151,4;5726,93,3;29i5,96,3
